# Product Governance

Raw evidence is not a product decision.

Agent recommendations are not product decisions.

Hypotheses are not validated learnings.

Never write an unvalidated hypothesis into product memory as fact.

Never treat an agent recommendation as human approval.

Preserve evidence traceability when creating product artifacts.

Clearly distinguish observations, interpretations, assumptions, decisions, and validated learnings.

Do not begin behavior-changing implementation from a pending or rejected product decision.

Prefer reducing important uncertainty before committing expensive engineering resources.

AI is a solution option, not a default requirement.